.TH P3M-CH 1 "@DATE@" "p3m @VERSION@" "p3m Manual"
.SH NAME
p3m-ch \- parallel chmod, chown and chgrp in a single scan
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B p3m-ch
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.IR PATH ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B p3m-ch
changes mode, owner and group across directory trees in one multi-threaded
recursive traversal.
The named
.IR PATH s
themselves are processed too.
.PP
Without
.B \-\-apply
this is a
.B dry run
that only lists the changes which would be made, as CSV.
Only entries whose metadata actually differs generate system calls, so
re-running on a compliant tree is nearly free and the dry run is an exact
preview.
.PP
At least one of
.BR \-m ", " \-f ", " \-d ", " \-u ", " \-g
is required.
Ownership is changed before mode so that set-id bits land as specified.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Mode and ownership
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " \fIMODE\fR"
Mode for both files and directories.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file\-mode " \fIMODE\fR"
Mode for files only (overrides
.B \-m
for files).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dir\-mode " \fIMODE\fR"
Mode for directories only (overrides
.B \-m
for directories).
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-owner " \fIUSER\fR"
New owner, as a name or numeric uid.
.IR USER : GROUP
is also accepted.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-group " \fIGROUP\fR"
New group, as a name or numeric gid.
.PP
.I MODE
is octal (\fB775\fR, \fB0775\fR, \fB2755\fR) or symbolic as in
.BR chmod (1):
clauses of
.RB [ ugoa ]([ +\-= ][ rwxXst ]|[ +\-= ][ ugo ])+
separated by commas, for example
.BR u+rwx,g\-w ,
.BR o=rx ,
.BR a+X ,
.BR g=u ,
.BR +t .
.SS Execution
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Make the changes (the default is a dry run).
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " \fIN\fR"
Worker threads (default: the number of online CPUs).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write the CSV change list to
.I FILE
and show a live progress display.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the console listing; progress and the summary are still shown, and a
.B \-o
file is still written.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
CSV rows list each entry that differs, with the old and new mode, owner and
group and a result column.
.SH SAFETY
Symbolic links are never followed.
Modes are never changed on links themselves (Linux does not support it), but
ownership is (via
.BR lchown (2)).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Errors were encountered.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Preview normalising a tree to 755/644:
.PP
.RS
.nf
p3m\-ch \-d 0755 \-f 0644 /srv/www
.fi
.RE
.PP
Apply it, together with an ownership change, in one pass:
.PP
.RS
.nf
p3m\-ch \-\-apply \-d 0755 \-f 0644 \-u www:www /srv/www
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR p3m (7),
.BR p3m\-find (1),
.BR chmod (1),
.BR chown (1),
.BR chgrp (1)
